hart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8ab5624d72209fbf81a960e50dd160402968c6900dd4fce7ef421796768b4d7b","event_uuid":"7c16f26c-8265-4bd9-a8c7-ca5fc0b6ce45","position":{"commit_sha":"5f3ad4c8491e765e0d701cfd2dcc18da3840d17b","position":"1785399131536330001-7c16f26c-8265-4bd9-a8c7-ca5fc0b6ce45"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2688a3a82248d029e31142ac5a3bf32a40410eeb96c1021879d4f10fe767f734","event_uuid":"3127a4d9-ab12-4c8d-95a7-b0fa5fa0fd54","position":{"commit_sha":"5f3ad4c8491e765e0d701cfd2dcc18da3840d17b","position":"1785399131983637001-3127a4d9-ab12-4c8d-95a7-b0fa5fa0fd54"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3baee7af9fbe5568cc3917a266d287953d8740052eca76b538dbaff2543d44b5","event_uuid":"958b8b01-b10f-4feb-9469-a4174c8bc39b","position":{"commit_sha":"3ad8b0e84e7af65203a5fd0793f443e8dda034a3","position":"1785399452845024952-958b8b01-b10f-4feb-9469-a4174c8bc39b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[],"created_at":1785384355519377001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"50276d8c-e7bd-43c3-b957-1932d5a5ac24","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bb9a-140f-9429-4034"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe runner attaches per-call usage to every result (`result[\"_usage\"]`, src/rebar/llm/runner.py:543) but Pass-1 discards it: passes.pass1_chunk, passes.pass1_container, and passes.pass1_isf return findings lists only, so BatchRunResult.outputs (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:167-176) carries no usage key and plan-review coverage.metrics has call counts but no token totals for the most expensive pass (the gap is documented at src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:139-149; _attach_plan_review_metrics currently reconstructs only det_ms/llm_ms/llm_calls timing proxies). Per-criterion request counts are extracted (runner.py:_extract_usage) but never persisted, blocking data-driven criterion demotion decisions.\n\n## Approach\nrun_pass1 does not call runner.run directly — calls flow through _chunk -> sizing.pass1_with_ladder -> passes.pass1_chunk (and the container/ISF variants). The usage is threaded through that chain as a coordinated API change with EVERY caller updated atomically in this one change. The three pass functions have consumers outside the plan_review package, all enumerated and updated here: the in-package chain (sizing.pass1_with_ladder chunk path, pass1._chunk, pass1's container fan-out via _timed_pairing, pass1's ISF invocation) plus src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py (pass1_container at line 120, pass1_chunk at line 137), src/rebar/llm/workflow/criterion_preview.py (pass1_chunk at line 345), and src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py (pass1 calls and the run_focused_finder 2-tuple destructure at line 344) — the eval/preview call sites unpack and discard the new usage element (`findings, _usage = ...`). Specifics: (1) passes.pass1_chunk, passes.pass1_container, and passes.pass1_isf change return type from list[dict] to (list[dict], dict) — findings plus the call's _usage dict; _timed_pairing keeps its existing (findings, pairing_record, exc) triple — the container call's usage is embedded as pairing_record[\"usage\"] so the observability record and the accumulator read one field. summarize_for_isf (passes.py:525-541) is a mode=\"text\" single-turn call returning a plain string (str(runner.run(req).get(\"text\", \"\"))) — it cannot return a pair without breaking its string contract, so it is handled differently: it changes to capture the full runner result internally and return (text, usage_dict), and its sole caller (the ISF oversized-log path in pass1.py) unpacks the pair and appends a call record attributed to the ISF criterion with criteria=[\"ISF\"]. sizing.pass1_with_ladder's two pass1_chunk call sites (the direct-return path at sizing.py:316 and the out.extend escalation path at sizing.py:333) both unpack the new pair and merge usage records. The concurrent-futures collector at pass1.py:490 changes from findings.extend(fu.result() or []) to unpacking: each future resolves to (findings_list, usage_records); the collector extends findings and appends the records. (2) Checkpoint fast-path: when sizing.load_checkpoint serves a chunk from cache, no LLM call happened — the chunk contributes NO call record and zero usage (a test asserts a checkpoint-resumed chunk adds nothing to the aggregate). Aggregation protocol: usage is recorded per CALL as {criteria: [ids the call covered], requests, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens} — no llm_calls field on a per-call record (one record IS one call); the per-criterion llm_calls value is DERIVED as the count of call records covering that criterion. Ladder retries: every COMPLETED attempt pass1_with_ladder makes for a chunk appends its own call record, all carrying the same criteria list. An attempt that RAISES (e.g. the context-limit error that triggers escalation) returns no result dict, so its usage is not recoverable from the current runner API — such attempts contribute nothing, and this limitation is documented in the accumulator's docstring; recovering usage from raising calls is explicitly out of scope. run_pass1 derives (a) the aggregate sum over all call records and (b) a per-criterion map using this attribution rule: an AGENT call (single criterion) attributes wholly to that criterion; a multi-criterion single-turn chunk attributes its token fields divided equally across its covered criteria (a documented approximation — the sidecar retains the raw per-call records, so exact attribution is always reconstructable), while the derived per-criterion llm_calls and the requests field count in full for each covered criterion. (3) The prerequisite finder runs in ProductionBatchRunner.run() via prerequisites.run_focused_finder, which returns (records, findings) with no usage — it is extended to return (records, findings, usage) where usage is the SUM over every runner.run call its internal run_bin closure makes (run_bin is recursive and multi-call; each call's _usage is accumulated inside run_focused_finder), its callers updated in the same change — ProductionBatchRunner.run and the fidelity_spot_eval.py destructure (scope includes src/rebar/llm/plan_review/prerequisites.py), and that usage is merged into the aggregate before emitting BatchRunResult.outputs[\"_usage\"]. (4) _attach_plan_review_metrics (src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:249+) is EXTENDED to fold the new token totals from the batch step output into coverage.metrics alongside its existing timing fields. (5) The sidecar payload (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py build_payload) gains coverage.usage = {\"per_call\": [call records], \"per_criterion\": {id: map}} — these exact key names are what the tests assert. Alternative rejected: post-hoc parsing of the REBAR_USAGE_LOG JSONL — opt-in, not always present, and not keyed by criterion.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py, src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py, src/rebar/llm/workflow/criterion_preview.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/prerequisites.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py, src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py (new, beside tests/unit/workflow/test_production_batch_runner.py).\n\n## Testing\nFakeRunner.run does not emit _usage (runner.py:134-151), so tests use a thin test-local wrapper runner that delegates to FakeRunner and attaches deterministic stub _usage dicts to each result — no change to FakeRunner itself. Unit with that wrapper: aggregate totals equal the sum over chunk, agent, container, ISF, and prerequisite call records; a two-criterion chunk with 100 input tokens attributes 50 to each criterion while counting one llm_call for each; a simulated ladder escalation whose first attempt completes yields two call records both counted, while a first attempt that raises contributes no record; coverage.usage.per_call and coverage.usage.per_criterion appear in the sidecar payload with the documented key names; coverage.metrics gains the token totals through the extended _attach_plan_review_metrics; a runner result without _usage degrades to zeros; the full existing pass1/batch-runner suites pass with the new return shapes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] After a review, coverage.metrics contains input/output/cache token totals that include Pass-1 and prerequisite calls (checked: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py` summing FakeRunner stub usage).\n- [ ] The sidecar payload carries coverage.usage.per_call (raw call records with criteria lists) and coverage.usage.per_criterion under exactly those keys (checked: sidecar payload unit test).\n- [ ] A multi-criterion chunk divides token fields equally across its criteria and counts llm_calls in full per criterion; ladder-retry attempts each contribute a call record (checked: dedicated unit tests for both rules).\n- [ ] Missing _usage on any call degrades to zero contribution (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] Every caller of the three changed pass functions and of run_focused_finder — including eval_solver.py, fidelity_spot_eval.py, and criterion_preview.py — is updated in this change and the existing pass1, batch-runner, eval, and finalize test suites pass unmodified in behavior (checked: full `pytest tests/unit/` run).\n- [ ] A checkpoint-resumed chunk contributes no usage and run_focused_finder's usage equals the sum over its internal run_bin calls (checked: dedicated unit tests).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py","reason":"return findings+usage pairs"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","reason":"propagate pair through ladder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py","reason":"aggregate + per-criterion usage; pairing_record usage"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/prerequisites.py","reason":"run_focused_finder usage sum"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","reason":"merge prerequisite usage; emit output"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py","reason":"coverage.usage payload"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"fold tokens into metrics"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py","reason":"caller unpack update"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py","reason":"caller unpack update"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/criterion_preview.py","reason":"caller unpack update"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","bb9a-140f-9429-4034"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"7c16f26c-8265-4bd9-a8c7-ca5fc0b6ce45","plan_review_phase":"execution"